    "turn_text": "You know how we know this, Sean? I give you one perfect microcosm of what happened leading up to this election that shows you they have no influence. So the same ABC News, after Kamala Harris became the Democratic nominee, the Media Research Center, looks at one hundred stories the first one hundred stories they did on kamala harris that train wreck of a campaign and they found that all one hundred were positive overall kamala harris got seventy eight percent positive coverage and the worst campaign we've ever seen yet that eight and ten stories are positive donald trump only got fifteen percent positive coverage Who won the popular vote? Who won every swing state? What party took back the Senate? What party held the House? Yeah, that's Donald Trump, Donald Trump, Republican and Republican. Those four answers in that order. So yeah, the influence is not fair at all. And it wasn't even, it was starting to go, you know, you declare media was dead back in 2007, 2008 with Barack Obama or from Bernie Goldberg wrote that great book, a slobbering love affair when they talked about the media coverage then. It didn't even get pale in comparison to what we just saw with this election, and yet Kamala Harris suffered an historic defeat because you're right. No one trusts the messenger anymore. And you're right. Some will come back, but I think most realize there's a lot of other options out there. whether it be great radio shows like yours, whether it be podcasts like the OVON and Joe Rogan, Ben Shapiro, or maybe they'll just not come back at all and just do their own homework on X. Either way, I think MSNBC will be sold off. I think CNN is going to see massive layoffs and a lot of other consolidation between media companies because if the ad revenue isn't coming in, that's how you get these guys' attention.",
